    <div class="street-inner">
      <div class="section-label-alt light">The Neighborhood</div>
      <h2>The last twelve months in Donnay's Valley Park.</h2>

      <div class="street-grid three">
        <div class="street-card">
          <div class="street-sold">36</div>
          <div class="street-meta">Homes sold here<br>in the last 12 months</div>
        </div>
        <div class="street-card">
          <div class="street-sold">14 days</div>
          <div class="street-meta">Average time<br>on market</div>
        </div>
        <div class="street-card">
          <div class="street-sold">102.6%</div>
          <div class="street-meta">Average sale price<br>versus list</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="street-takeaway">
        Four-bedroom homes around 1,900 square feet from this era have gone from about <strong>$190 a square foot in 2024</strong> to <strong>$203 in 2026</strong>. $399,000 is priced on that trend, not ahead of it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE COMPETITION -->
  <section class="actives">
    <div class="section-label-alt">The Competition</div>
    <h2>What's on the market right now.</h2>
    <p class="actives-intro">
      Four-bedroom homes in the neighborhood today:
    </p>
    <ul class="actives-list">
      <li><strong>$389,900</strong> &nbsp;·&nbsp; 16515 Flagstaff Ave, a 1,786 sq ft four-bed, smaller than yours. <span class="dom-tag">active</span></li>
      <li><strong>$387,400</strong> &nbsp;·&nbsp; 16344 Fantasia Ave, 1,810 sq ft, a newer 1985 build on a smaller lot. <span class="dom-tag">active</span></li>
      <li><strong>$399,900</strong> &nbsp;·&nbsp; 16680 Galena Ave, a bigger 2,411 sq ft home listed $900 above you, already pending. <span class="dom-tag">pending</span></li>
    </ul>
